<!--
  THE VAULT themed-icon (monochrome) layer, Android 13+.

  THE BARBELL (v403, owner decision): the five rectangles of ICONS.dumbbell,
  placed exactly as ic_launcher_foreground.xml places them (scale 2.1, moved
  28.8, the glyph's centre on 54,54), so the themed icon and the coloured one
  are the same shape. Contract 72 holds it there.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM ic_launcher_foreground.xml. A launcher
  renders the monochrome layer from its ALPHA CHANNEL ONLY and tints the whole
  thing one wallpaper colour, so the foreground's three fills would flatten to
  one anyway. Here the mark is one white silhouette: ONE path of five
  subpaths, so the shaft, which abuts both inner plates, is rasterised with
  them as a single union and no seam of background can show along the join.

  No evenOdd: every part of the barbell is ink, and there is no hole to cut
  (the old V needed one for its slot). The two gaps between each outer and
  inner plate are empty canvas, not shapes, so they survive the tint.

  BAKED INTO THE APK: nothing here reaches a phone until build 25 is installed.
-->
